1. npm i @monaco-editor/react //you can put a VS Code-like code editor inside your React website.

2. npm i socket.io //Used for real-time communication between the frontend and backend.

3. npm i y-socket.io  //This is related to Yjs, a framework for building collaborative applications.
For example, imagine you are building a website like Google Docs or a collaborative code editor.
Two users can edit the same document

4. npm i cors //Installs the CORS package so your backend can allow requests from different frontend origins/domains.

5. useState //Stores data/state in a component and re-renders the component when that data changes.

6. useEffect // Runs code after the component renders, usually for side effects like API calls, timers, or event listeners.

7. useRef //Stores a value or references a DOM element without causing a re-render when it changes.

8. useMemo // Caches the result of an expensive calculation and recalculates it only when its dependencies change.

9. SocketIOProvider  //creates and manages a Socket.IO connection so multiple components can communicate and receive real-time updates through the same connection.

10. Yjs // is a JavaScript library used to make real-time collaboration possible.